WEBVTT

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:37.360
For a boy to say...

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:41.420
"I'm taking the girl I like to a super fun amusement park for her to enjoy"...

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.830
...is not a very difficult thing.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.870
A quick check of the times for events and fireworks in a guide...

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.530
...and you go off happily together.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.310
However...

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:54.480
"I'm going to MAKE a super fun amusement park for the girl I like to enjoy"...

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.580
...is quite a large undertaking.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.220
By the time you can do it properly, you'll be a pro among pros.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.120
You're certain to come to be called an entertainment specialist.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.110
Of course, by then, the girl may not necessarily be by your side.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.820
Well, in the case of Sasshi, a child and an amateur...

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.330
...it's only natural that he wasn't able to do a good job.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.890
What else could you expect?

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:20.860
Wars happen because they are meant to happen.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.620
There exists a cause and a goal.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.580
The war between the Turtle Bath Army and the Pelican Army...

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:34.340
...which broke out at the Abenobashi Shopping Arcade, was no exception.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.780
Arumi desperately wishes to return to her own world...

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.290
...but Sasshi does not, because he has learned of Masa-jii's death.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:46.350
It was inevitable that they would confront each other and clash.

00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.920
Their showdown turned into a war of attrition...

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.960
...and as a result, the battle line has been deadlocked.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:42.570
Message!

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.650
Private E-1 Sasshi of Squad 7, Corps 6 of District 5 General HQ...

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:48.260
...auxiliary to the 4th Battalion, under command of the 3rd Regiment...

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.910
...under the 2nd Division, of the 1st Army, reporting, ma'am.

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:54.790
State your posting.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.260
What? I just said it.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.750
State your posting!

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:00.430
Let's see...

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.960
Private E-1 Sasshi of Squad 7, Corps 6 of District 5 General HQ...

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:06.570
I can't say it twice, ma'am!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:08.810
Good.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:09.610
It's okay?

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:10.520
Report!

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:11.850
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.450
A tank unit of the enemy Pelican Army...

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:15.850
...is assembling in front of the Wakaba Cigarette Shop. End of report!

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.590
I see, good work.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.850
Communicate that to Division Headquarters immediately!

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:21.920
Me, ma'am?!

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:24.480
Of course! Go, now!

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:25.360
Yes, ma'am!

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:41.710
Message...

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.480
Private E-1 Sasshi of Squad 7, Army Corps 6 of Region 5 General HQ...

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:51.450
...oh, auxiliary to the 4th Battalion, under command of the 3rd Regiment...

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:55.450
...under the 2nd Division, of the 1st Army, reporting, sir.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.360
I see, a tank unit of the enemy Pelican Army...

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.330
...is assembling in front of the Wakaba Cigarette Shop.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.030
Unbelievable!

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.870
I ain't said nothing yet.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.070
Good work!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.570
Please let General Headquarters know right away.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.500
Wha?! Me, sir?!

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:10.870
Of course!

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:11.640
Yes, sir!

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.250
Go, now!

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:36.600
Message...

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.260
Uh, yeah...

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.360
Private E-1 Sasshi of Squad 7...

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.440
You are Private E-1 Sasshi of Squad 7...

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.780
...Army Corps 6 of Region 5 General Headquarters...

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.710
...auxiliary to the 4th Battalion, under command of the 3rd Regiment...

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:52.340
...under the 2nd Division, of the 1st Army.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:55.150
What? Are you Private E-1 Sasshi of Squad 7...

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:57.480
...Army Corps 6 of Region 5 General Headquarters...

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.520
...auxiliary to the 4th Battalion, under command of the 3rd Regiment...

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.170
...under the 2nd Division, of the 1st Army?

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:04.290
Yes.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.490
Good, you may return.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.000
But I haven't made my report yet.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.200
General, a tank unit of the enemy Pelican Army...

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.190
...is apparently assembling in front of the Wakaba Cigarette Shop.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.930
What?! In front of the Wakaba Cigarette Shop?!

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:17.710
Am I actually of any use here?

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.900
All right, run the message to Forward HQ, Private E-1 Sasshi!

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:30.840
It's the same sort of thing day after day after day.

00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:35.280
I wonder how long this war's gonna go on for?

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.230
Now is indeed the time to deliver a righteous and crushing blow...

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:47.170
...to those incompetent bastards of the Turtle Bath Army!

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.840
Senior General Papa!

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:49.680
Oui.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.940
You will lead the armored division...

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.610
...penetrate the trenches in one fell swoop...

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:55.130
...and strike at the enemy command headquarters!

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:59.170
Make a grand display of your skills in the art of war!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:00.650
Oui.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:01.650
Colonel Arumi!

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:02.190
Yes, sir!

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.900
I appoint you to be Senior General Papa's aide.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.260
With all due respect, I decline to be nothing but a simple aide.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:11.690
Please assign my unit to the vanguard!

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.160
Well spoken.

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:14.910
That is why our army is so strong!

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:16.910
Abeno shall be ours!

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.370
Abeno shall be ours!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.970
What are they, USO?

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:26.870
C'mon, c'mon, it's cheap, it's cheap! Come and buy some!

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:29.370
I've got everything from rifles to bombers!

00:07:29.580 --> 00:07:31.670
You can buy anything as long as you have money!

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.610
Hey, Sasshi, buy something!

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.750
Sorry, Kouhei-san, I've only got 100 yen.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:37.720
One, two, three...

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.220
Then have some dumpling soup!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.690
Here, 100 yen for a bowl.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.190
That looks tasty.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.390
But I'm curious 'bout the USO choppers, too...

00:07:44.390 --> 00:07:45.590
What? USO choppers?

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:46.630
Yeah.

00:07:52.030 --> 00:07:53.500
It's the USO, just like I thought!

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.110
Gulp.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.550
Oh, dear!

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.800
My goodness, are you that happy to see me?

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:17.320
Flatterers.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.520
I'll guide everyone...

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.850
...to Heaven.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:26.060
Don't you mean Hell?

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.730
Hello, everyone.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:30.970
Starting now...

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.440
I'll be singing and dancing for the next two and a half hours.

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:35.310
Please sit back and enjoy...

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:46.490
Well, there's no doubt he was a dangerous object.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:48.360
Private E-1 Sasshi!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.840
Yes, what is it, ma'am?!

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:53.340
Private E-1 Sasshi, you are hereby assigned to scouting duty.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:54.550
That is all.

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:56.550
Yes, ma'am!

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:05.700
Private E-1 Sasshi, be quiet!

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:07.670
Please forgive me, ma'am!

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.010
But Major, ma'am, perhaps you should slow down a little...

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:12.810
This is nothing, we're just getting started!

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.820
I have a bad feeling about this!

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:26.000
Hey!

00:09:27.430 --> 00:09:28.000
Arumi!

00:09:28.530 --> 00:09:30.000
I've found ya, Sasshi!

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.960
Whoa, Arumi, why d'you got such big breasts?

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.300
Eek! You noticed it already.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.440
Non, non, non!

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:40.740
Private, you still haven't gotten the "meaning" of this tank unit.

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.410
You pad Arumi's breasts and now, it's really a "Padton Tank" unit...

00:09:46.250 --> 00:09:49.230
Yeah, right. It can't be something that stupid.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.730
What? You went to all that trouble for something that pointless?

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:57.530
This is why I didn't wanna say it.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:10:00.490
If you didn't wanna, then don't do it to start with.

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:04.470
There's more. These pads are actually gold, ya know.

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:05.360
"Golden pad."

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:06.960
He's saying the lines before you get to them again.

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.770
C'mon, laugh...

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.030
Don't cry, it's depressing.

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.810
Why are you talking so imperiously to me, Arumi-chan?

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:17.000
I can't believe I have to fight under a general like him.

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.880
It's such an ordeal.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:20.150
That's my line!

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:21.120
Goodbye.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.280
Why the heck are we so good?

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:24.600
Don't go back in!

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:28.590
And quit it with the accompaniment!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.600
Don't make me do these nonsensical things!

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.660
I am totally ticked now!

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:34.060
Eat this!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:43.580
Since it's come to this...

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.080
Major, ma'am?!

00:10:46.410 --> 00:10:48.310
Private E-1 Sasshi, you understand, don't you?

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:51.570
If you want to protect someone, sometimes, sacrifices become necessary.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:53.090
You mean...

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.260
Don't forget about me, okay?

00:10:56.850 --> 00:10:57.510
Nee-chan!

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.250
Sasshi, farewell.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:08.060
Sasshi, I'll never forget the sacrifice you made.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:09.490
I just knew it!

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.760
Protecting your superior officer is a subordinate's duty!

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:12.990
Bye-bye!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.870
You trying to kill me?!

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:23.500
It's always something like this.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.400
Haha, Sasshi! How d'you like that?!

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.080
This is the Red Tiger of Kamchatka.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.830
White Rabbit of Inaba, go ahead.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:42.460
A large-scale black wolf is closing in on our position.

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.830
<i>White Rabbit to Red Tiger.</i>

00:11:44.830 --> 00:11:46.970
<i>Battalion cannons, regiment cannons, division cannons...</i>

00:11:46.970 --> 00:11:48.640
<i>...all units capable of providing reinforcement.</i>

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.540
Red Tiger to White Rabbit.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:52.600
Bombard them without delay.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:54.870
<i>White Rabbit, roger that. Commence barrage!</i>

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.030
Non!

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:08.880
We did it!

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:31.850
Well done, Private E-1 Sasshi.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.300
No, after being specially promoted three ranks, as of now, you are Sergeant Sasshi.

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:36.480
What? For real?

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.420
This time, it is our turn to go on the offensive.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:42.960
On the offensive?

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:43.620
Yes, ma'am!

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.560
We execute a great surprise attack with our anti-air power!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.620
It doesn't matter what it is, we just do it!

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:51.630
All right, it's sudden and I don't really understand it, but I understand!

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:53.360
We will use your idea.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:55.900
Where is the enemy's main force at this time?

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.500
The scout plane is searching for them.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.010
Message from the scout plane.

00:12:59.010 --> 00:13:01.200
The enemy's main force is assembled at the barber shop.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:02.940
At the barber shop, you say?!

00:13:03.140 --> 00:13:04.450
All right, Major Sayaka.

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:06.250
Sergeant Sasshi will launch a surprise attack on that location!

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:08.340
It's all or nothing! We will settle everything now!

00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.930
Yes, ma'am! We will do our very best!

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:25.900
No anti-air response. And no enemy interceptors coming up.

00:13:26.770 --> 00:13:28.500
Okay! The surprise attack is a success!

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:30.900
Tiger, Tiger, Tiger's gold coin dumplings!

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:34.440
Follow me! I'll show them the might of rapidly descending bombers!

00:13:50.290 --> 00:13:54.300
Whoa, that's the later version of the dog god statue...

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.700
...the secret animal in the second set of choco-eggs...

00:13:56.700 --> 00:13:58.960
...lost in the non-amicable split between two certain companies!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.460
Changing target!

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:08.470
Operation successful.

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:11.330
But I didn't think it'd be successful for real...

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:12.620
What a moron.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:23.920
As of now, you are assigned the rank of captain.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:26.560
Excuse me, but why do I get to be promoted?

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.660
I do not really understand either.

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:30.460
Maybe it's 'cause our numbers are diminshing.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:31.770
Oh, really.

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.460
<i>Imperial headquarters, air force announcement.</i>

00:14:36.570 --> 00:14:38.940
<i>In the Battle at Pearl Barber, which just took place...</i>

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.580
<i>...our side attained victory.</i>

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:43.950
<i>In this engagement, Sergeant Sasshi distinguished himself...</i>

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:46.110
<i>...fighting like a demon, and was granted the unprecedented honor...</i>

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.020
<i>...of a five rank promotion to captain.</i>

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:48.020
We're probably gonna lose this war.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.250
Did you say something?

00:14:49.250 --> 00:14:49.950
No, nothing.

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:53.960
We absolutely, absolutely cannot lose this war!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:57.330
We must defend this place, the Turtle Bath, at all costs!

00:14:57.330 --> 00:15:00.390
It's terrible! The enemy has moved! The Tsutenkaku...

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:01.460
What?!

00:15:24.890 --> 00:15:27.750
Since it's come to this, I will deliver the coup de grace myself!

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:30.050
With this giant battleship, Yamatogawa!

00:15:30.560 --> 00:15:33.230
Radar readings confirmed! Multiple enemy fighters!

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:33.910
Rout them!

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:49.420
It's no use! Every last unit in the assault force has been shot down!

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.130
Isn't this getting seriously bad?

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:53.500
Incoming message from the enemy!

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.910
To the commander of the Turtle Bath Army, General Mune-mune.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:59.350
You people have fought well.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.790
However, the might of my battleship Yamatogawa is colossal.

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.860
Your military strength cannot compare!

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.570
You should know that better than anyone else.

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.360
You do not even have a one in a million chance of winning.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.360
So, General Mune-mune...

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.540
Please marry me!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.940
What's he saying?

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:20.770
Sorry 'bout the joke.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.040
You guys have weak knees and backs.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:27.680
Anyway, if you are willing to surrender, I will happily accept.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:29.880
As of now, you have a five-minute grace period.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.590
However, I will make one thing clear!

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:35.420
Listen well, we are...

00:16:37.630 --> 00:16:39.060
Speak clearly!

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.100
What shall we do, General?

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.800
Tell them, "You fools."

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.350
I said, "You fools!"

00:16:44.670 --> 00:16:45.630
"You fools."

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:47.490
Whoa, he's mad now.

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:50.860
C'mon, laugh.

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.770
Why you! The one who calls another a fool is the fool!

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:54.860
All cannons at the ready!

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.830
What shall we do?!

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:08.040
We have not lost yet.

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:10.350
We have a final resort to fall back on.

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:11.950
Final resort?

00:17:31.710 --> 00:17:32.680
Fire!

00:17:57.540 --> 00:17:58.630
Where is everyone?

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.180
We're done for now! Help!

00:18:09.850 --> 00:18:12.150
This is nothing! We'll just have to fall back on our final resort!

00:18:12.590 --> 00:18:13.720
There's still more?!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:14.780
We'll have to get in close!

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:17.550
Get in close?!

00:18:24.430 --> 00:18:26.330
That man will return without fail.

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.500
The Turtle Bath must hold out until he comes back!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:32.300
Huh? What?

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.010
We're charging!

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.510
Charging a warship in the flesh?

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:37.740
Come!

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:42.620
Stop! Stop! We're gonna die! We're gonna die! We're gonna die!

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.190
Die fighting!

00:18:44.190 --> 00:18:45.620
No way! I don't wanna die!

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.620
Can you die for someone else?!

00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:48.620
No, I can't! No, I can't!

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:50.860
Cosmo-zone of love!

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:52.620
I don't understand!

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:09.680
I'm happy that her breasts are pressed against my back, but...

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:15.240
Mune-mune, don't die!

00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:19.210
Mune-mune, hang on!

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.190
Don't worry...

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:28.520
Because I haven't, I haven't seem him yet...

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.640
Mune-mune...

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.060
Sasshi, how is our battle progressing?

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.830
We're doing fine! Our side's winning!

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:38.410
Really?

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.240
Yeah, for real! So, hang in there, Mune-mune!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.080
The Turtle Bath will be protected...

00:19:45.810 --> 00:19:47.610
Once again, he'll...

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.520
Mune-mune?

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:53.480
I have faith that as long as the Turtle Bath is still here...

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:56.580
...he will come to me again.

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.560
Mune-mune...

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:03.660
I'm sure, I'm sure that if I just believe, it will come true...

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:05.600
If I just believe...

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:08.500
Yeah, that's right. Of course, you're...

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:12.460
As long as you believe, there's nothing you can't do. Nothing.

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:15.770
Sasshi, thank you.

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:19.860
You have to live, with your own strength now.

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:20.860
Mune-mune.

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:26.680
Oh, I can see his face smiling. He's...

00:20:29.690 --> 00:20:30.660
Mune-mune?!

00:20:30.990 --> 00:20:33.320
Mune-mune!

00:20:46.710 --> 00:20:48.830
There was no shopping arcade there.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:50.970
All that had been was in ruins.

00:20:51.450 --> 00:20:54.110
In this land that had suffered the ultimate in destruction...

00:20:54.110 --> 00:20:56.740
...there was no sound and no movement.

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:58.790
Sasshi understood then...

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:02.380
...that a shopping arcade in this world was now dead.

00:21:03.320 --> 00:21:04.950
War is meaningless.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.290
An excerpt from Sasshi Imamiya's memoirs...

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.160
Chapter 3 of the introduction.

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:13.460
Well, it was interesting, but it's been kinda rough, too.

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:16.070
I guess there's no place like home. I wanna go home.

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:19.370
I heard ya, I heard ya!

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:21.070
You just said, you wanna go home!

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:22.880
What?

00:21:24.080 --> 00:21:26.650
Haven't you had enough? I've had tons of fun already.

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.710
I've enjoyed some of it in my own way too.

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:29.880
Really?

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:31.020
Think 'bout it for a second.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:35.320
Just 'cause I'm going to Hokkaido doesn't mean we'll never see each other again.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.860
And there's nothing better than living in good health in our own world...

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:41.320
...rather than keep wandering from one stupid world to another. Right?

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:45.260
If you just believe, it will come true...

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.280
Yeah!

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:50.530
Yeah, she might be right.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.910
All right, let's go with that then!

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:57.290
Shall we go home?

00:21:57.880 --> 00:21:58.790
Yeah!

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:03.810
With my powers, we may be able to jump to a world where Masa-jii's alive and well.

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:07.590
No, I can make the jump. I'm sure I can!

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:09.180
I gotta believe!

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:48.490
Now, in the next episode of Magical Shopping Arcade Abenobashi...

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:48.490
Oh, my, Arumi, what are you doing, dear?

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:52.260
After all the fun war games resulted in a sad ending...

00:23:48.490 --> 00:23:51.560
Oh, Aki-nee. Sasshi's doing the next episode preview right now.

00:23:51.560 --> 00:23:53.390
Oh, preview du delelemont.

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:54.500
Sasshi finally feels like going home.

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:54.500
I'll do it!

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:55.760
I wanna do the preview!

00:23:55.360 --> 00:23:57.760
They think they have returned to their world at last...

00:23:55.760 --> 00:23:58.000
Wow, a ton of people are showing up today for some reason.

00:23:58.000 --> 00:23:59.370
I've been thinking this for a while now...

00:23:58.300 --> 00:24:03.000
...but strangely enough, it was yet another strange world after all.

00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:01.240
...but every single time, they're such haphazard previews...

00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:03.000
...or rather, I don't think they serve as previews at all.

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:04.540
Are ya okay with this sorta thing, Mr. Director?

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:06.740
What could possibly be awaiting in this next world?

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:06.740
Well, I'm not the one writing the previews...

00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:09.140
...it's some little scribblings from this guy from Akashi...

00:24:07.270 --> 00:24:10.410
Next time, "Huge Reversal?! Abenobashi Hollywood Shopping Arcade."

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:10.410
Oh, I wanna do the preview!

00:24:10.410 --> 00:24:11.850
Please look forward to it. There.

00:24:10.410 --> 00:24:11.850
Preview! Preview! Preview!

00:24:11.850 --> 00:24:13.250
Mune-chan, you certainly are enthusiastic.

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:14.050
Hello?

00:24:14.050 --> 00:24:15.050
Oh, brother.
